    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d373">

                <pb facs="0668" n="568" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg568"/>

                <head>No. 373.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoppin to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 27, 1880</date>.
                        (Received March 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 156.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I received late last evening your telegram,
                    without date, stating that you learned with increased chagrin, from my No. 147,
                    of even a possible further delay of one month in the answer to our Fortune Bay
                    claims, and instructing me to urge its avoidance if possible. I have,
                    accordingly, addressed Lord Salisbury again on this subject, and herewith
                    inclose a copy of my note to his lordship.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. J. HOPPIN.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d373-a1.xml" xpointer="d373-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
